---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_URL, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy policy of AdmitCost: no account, no student profile kept" description="What the admissions and net price calculators process: no cookie, no account, no score or family income stored or sent. Your rights under US state privacy laws and the GDPR." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This policy covers {SITE_URL}. Many "chances" tools exist to build lists of students for consultants and recruiters. This one was built so that it never needs to know who you are. The publisher is established in France: the EU General Data Protection Regulation applies to everything the site does, for every visitor, and residents of US states with a consumer privacy law keep at least the rights listed here.</p>
    <p>No cookie is set by this site and the calculators store nothing on your device.</p>
    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>2. What stays in your browser</h2>
    <p>The university you pick, your SAT or ACT score, your family income and your state of residence are used only by the calculation running in your own browser. Nothing is sent to us or to anyone else. The "copy share link" button writes these inputs into the page address so you can send the result; whoever receives the link can read them.</p>
    <h2>3. What is processed</h2>
    <h3>Hosting logs</h3><p>Like every web host, GitHub records the IP address, time, page requested and browser type of each request to keep the service secure. Legal basis: legitimate interest. Retention follows GitHub's own policy.</p>
    {CLARITY_ID
      ? <><h3>Anonymous stability monitoring, without cookies</h3><p>To find broken pages and scripts, the site loads Microsoft Clarity (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, Dublin) in its cookie-free mode: errors, loading times, dead clicks and scrolling are measured per page view, without cookies and without linking visits; page content and everything you type are masked. Microsoft receives the technical data of the request, including the IP address. Legal basis: legitimate interest in a working site (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). You can object by blocking clarity.ms or by writing to us.</p></>
      : <><h3>No analytics</h3><p>No audience measurement, analytics, advertising or social media tool is loaded today. If a stability monitoring tool is added, this page will name it and explain what it records before it is switched on.</p></>}
    <h3>E-mails</h3><p>If you write to us, we keep your address and message to answer, and delete them three years after the last exchange. You never need to send a score or an income to report a figure.</p>
    <h2>4. No sale, no sharing, no student lists</h2><p>We do not sell or share personal information, pass anything to universities, consultants, lenders or recruiters, or build profiles.</p>
    <h2>5. Recipients and transfers</h2><p>The host, GitHub, Inc., is in the United States; request data may be processed there under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>You may ask for access, correction, deletion, restriction or portability, or object to processing, by writing to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we answer within one month. You may also complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>).</p>
    <h2>7. Children and teenagers</h2><p>Many readers are high school students. The site collects nothing from anyone, so there is nothing to collect from a child under 13 either; a student can use every calculator without giving a name, an age or an e-mail address.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a> and the <a href={route('terms', lang)}>legal notice</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
